SWEET WLAN run F2 (patch 0135, docs/research/53-wd4-msgbuf-ring-plan.md s5.2), boot-arg sweetwlan=9 = level 8 (patch 0134, unchanged: same log, reads and stores) + more READ-ONLY dumps of the halted firmware's RAM through BAR2 window 0. No new store, no new mapping, no cfg 0x84 store, no new read row.
Why: on hardware (run F1, wlan-runF1-0134, observed) the console (0x3b19d8), the mailbox data words (0x3ed8b4, 0x3ed8b8) and rings_info_ptr (0x3ed578) are below 0x400000, so swl_f1_span_ok refused them in the tail window (review 0134 F3).
What: swl_f2() runs in W17 after the CA7 re-halt and the cfg 0x84 := 0 restore row (restore ended ok), before the PCIe core group: mailbox data (2 words), ring_info (19), the 5 ring_mem entries (80 B), the console (hnd_cons_t, up to 4 KiB, same 128 lines x 120 chars caps), each pointer through swl_f1_span_ok with window 0. Guard: cfg 0x84 reads 0 and the RAM word at 0x200000 still equals word 0 of the pinned image (the shared word is in the tail window and cannot be re-read without a store); both printed. Stops (all-ones block of 2+ words, failed read or precondition) happen with nothing armed.
Glue: level 9 accepted, named "F2"; rev gate (level >= 7) unchanged. HW-WRITE path: unreviewed (read-only additions to a reviewed path).

